                "entry_id": "f4a3976c-ae39-3f25-a423-8f83907d4222",
                "word": "aphobie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c67a2577-4df2-4229-99af-c6b31709de81",
                        "entry_id": "f4a3976c-ae39-3f25-a423-8f83907d4222",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "aphobies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc25d630-587f-3eeb-9369-371b0aa55b4b",
                        "entry_id": "f4a3976c-ae39-3f25-a423-8f83907d4222",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Discrimination, aversion envers les personnes asexuelles et/ou aromantiques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f96b4539-9b7f-46df-8efa-63fef22edf11",
                                "sense_id": "bc25d630-587f-3eeb-9369-371b0aa55b4b",
                                "text": "Donc oui, lʼaphobie est majoritairement alimentée par le sexisme/patriarcat et ce sont les femmes ace qui morflent le +. Mais si c’est votre excuse pour jeter l’aphobie par la fenêtre, on fait pareil pour la lesbophobie et d’autres types de queerphobie qui concernent des femmes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b07c5361-6d8b-4f98-a006-500523d573ae",
                                "sense_id": "bc25d630-587f-3eeb-9369-371b0aa55b4b",
                                "text": "Je suis sidérée de l’aphobie vraiment, pourquoi ???\n Je pense que je savais depuis hyper longtemps que j'étais aro ace juste je refusais de me l’avouer\n On nait comme ça donc oui à 14 ans on peut le savoir"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3e6bc6a-895d-4afc-ab04-239d184410c5",
                                "sense_id": "bc25d630-587f-3eeb-9369-371b0aa55b4b",
                                "text": "Y a pas mal de personnes qui m’ont suivie suite à mon dessin nul donc rappel : je suis asexuelle et aromantique et si vous pensez que l’aphobie n’existe pas nos chemins n'étaient pas censés se croiser"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8bf228fd-c235-4d53-b8ee-b2db4504d953",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4a3976c-ae39-3f25-a423-8f83907d4222",
                        "source_sense_id": "bc25d630-587f-3eeb-9369-371b0aa55b4b",
                        "target_lang_word": "aphobia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aphobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8701adcc-af7b-3111-b844-e69157a8aa80",
                                        "entry_id": "4b2f8a38-ddef-321f-96f3-e166c5dcc57c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fearlessness or lack of fear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86461855-5415-443a-9be6-398dbf7ac6b9",
                                                "sense_id": "8701adcc-af7b-3111-b844-e69157a8aa80",
                                                "text": "Similar ones occurring daily in a large metropolis like ours, where aphobia for operations walks extant and can be easily acquired."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef439096-d86e-47f0-aae0-a89469585eb1",
                                                "sense_id": "8701adcc-af7b-3111-b844-e69157a8aa80",
                                                "text": "Put the body into a state of aphobia, fearlessness, the Spartans believe, and the mind will follow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f63edee-3e47-4bd5-8162-ab6c2f11d362",
                                                "sense_id": "8701adcc-af7b-3111-b844-e69157a8aa80",
                                                "text": "I find joy and meaning in my life when I embrace life with aphobia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "aphobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eae4bc1e-9810-30bf-82f3-db9769a13141",
                                        "entry_id": "22dbe374-0d11-32b3-be75-874f9cfa3d16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fear, dislike, or hatred of asexual and/or aromantic people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "neologism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ec299db-023a-4a1f-ae55-ba6c72dcb9b7",
                                                "sense_id": "eae4bc1e-9810-30bf-82f3-db9769a13141",
                                                "text": "Where aphobia goes wrong is that it assumes that some ace people 'pass' as straight, and therefore experience no discrimination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "666099a6-5c7b-42bb-8dd9-f9bb109cf818",
                                                "sense_id": "eae4bc1e-9810-30bf-82f3-db9769a13141",
                                                "text": "This should've been the moment I shucked off the last fetter of my internalised aphobia and claimed my asexuality as my own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6901c1ae-a95f-48ff-8d68-ba63b47ad0e9",
                                                "sense_id": "eae4bc1e-9810-30bf-82f3-db9769a13141",
                                                "text": "If you can recognize the mircoagressions we've discussed here and their variants in the world, you can spot aphobia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
